---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { canteen, arc, groundedThemes } from '../../data/partners/index';

// The corpus table renders every theme in the data, not a selected few: a theme
// with no authored benchmark task shows no count rather than a zero, so the
// coverage gap is visible instead of hidden.
const themes = canteen.corpus?.themes ?? [];
const grounded = groundedThemes(canteen);
const groundedTaskIds = new Set(grounded.flatMap((t) => t.taskIds ?? []));
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Canteen"
  description="Canteen runs Arc's public developer stack: a testnet node, a keyed JSON-RPC gateway, and the arc-canteen CLI. Their 370-project hackathon corpus is what the Arc benchmark's task content is drawn from."
  bodyClass="page-editorial"
>
  <section class="pt-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <a class="pt-back" href="/partners">&larr; Partners</a>
      <div class="pt-role mono">{canteen.role}</div>
      <h1>{canteen.name}</h1>
      <p class="pt-lede">
        Canteen is the New York firm that runs Arc's public developer stack, and the reason the Arc
        benchmark is about real work rather than invented exercises.
        They ran the hackathons that produced the corpus, and that corpus is where the task content
        comes from.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-facts mono">
        <span><strong>{canteen.corpus?.total}</strong> community projects</span>
        <span>across <strong>Lepton</strong> and <strong>Agora</strong></span>
        <span><strong>{grounded.length}</strong> themes carried into benchmark tasks</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pt-body">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="pt-block">
        <h2>The developer stack</h2>
        <p class="pt-p">
          Canteen operates the path a developer takes onto Arc. It matters to a benchmark because it
          is also the path a coding agent takes: the same key, the same endpoint, the same docs.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-method-grid">
          <div class="pt-m">
            <h3>A full Arc testnet node</h3>
            <p>
              Canteen runs the node the public developer stack is served from, rather than reselling
              someone else's endpoint.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-m">
            <h3>A keyed JSON-RPC gateway</h3>
            <p>
              Per-developer URLs at
              <span class="mono">rpc.testnet.arc-node.thecanteenapp.com</span>, with a method allowlist
              and tokens that rotate on a 90 day cycle. The allowlist and the rotation are what the
              gateway benchmark tasks are written against.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-m">
            <h3>The arc-canteen CLI</h3>
            <p>
              A GitHub login returns a funded testnet wallet, an RPC key, and the Arc documentation in
              a form that can be piped straight into a coding agent, so an agent starts with a working
              chain connection instead of a setup problem.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-m">
            <h3>An open-source showcase</h3>
            <p>
              Community projects are published rather than archived, which is what makes the corpus
              below readable as evidence of what people build on Arc.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-block">
        <h2>What the community actually built</h2>
        <p class="pt-p">
          Two hackathons, Lepton and Agora, produced {canteen.corpus?.total} projects. Tagging them
          gives a distribution rather than an anecdote, and that distribution is the reason the
          benchmark covers what it covers. Every theme is listed here, including the ones no benchmark
          task has been written for yet.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-receipts-scroll">
          <table class="pt-receipts">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Theme</th>
                <th>Projects</th>
                <th>Share of projects</th>
                <th>Arc benchmark tasks</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {themes.map((t) => (
                <tr>
                  <td class="pt-r-id">{t.theme}</td>
                  <td class="pt-r-num mono">{t.projects}</td>
                  <td class="pt-r-bar-cell">
                    <span class="pt-bar" style={`--f:${t.projects / (canteen.corpus?.total ?? 1)}`}></span>
                    <span class="pt-bar-val mono">{Math.round((t.projects / (canteen.corpus?.total ?? 1)) * 100)}%</span>
                  </td>
                  <td>
                    {t.tasks ? (
                      <span class="pt-task-ids mono">{(t.taskIds ?? []).join(', ')}</span>
                    ) : (
                      <span class="pt-none mono">none authored yet</span>
                    )}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="pt-note">
          Projects carry more than one tag, so the theme counts sum to more than the
          {' '}{canteen.corpus?.total} projects.
          Task columns count authored leaves in the <span class="mono">{arc.verticalId}</span> vertical
          carrying that tag, counted from
          <span class="mono">{arc.verticalSource}</span>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-block">
        <h2>How the corpus becomes a task</h2>
        <p class="pt-p">
          A benchmark that invents its own tasks measures whatever its author found interesting. The
          Arc tasks are drawn from the ranked themes above, so what the benchmark rewards is what the
          ecosystem is actually trying to build.
          Of the {arc.taskCount} tasks in the vertical, {groundedTaskIds.size} implement a pattern that
          appears in the corpus by name.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-rungs">
          {grounded.map((t) => (
            <div class="pt-rung pt-rung-tight">
              <div class="pt-rung-head">
                <h3>{t.theme}</h3>
                <span class="pt-rung-count mono">{t.projects} projects &middot; {t.tasks} task{t.tasks === 1 ? '' : 's'}</span>
              </div>
              <div class="pt-chips">
                {(t.taskIds ?? []).map((id) => <span class="pt-chip mono">{id}</span>)}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="pt-note">
          A theme with a large corpus count and no task is a gap we can name, which is the point of
          publishing the whole distribution rather than the part that matches.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-block" id="board">
        <h2>Canteen's own surface</h2>
        <p class="pt-p">
          The gateway and the CLI are also benchmarked, in a separate vertical about operational
          correctness rather than protocol design. Those tasks grade behaviour, not just return
          values: whether a client rotates a key once and retries once on an expired token but never
          retries a request the allowlist refused, and whether a queue that crashes mid replay can be
          replayed against an idempotent server without landing an event twice.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-pending">
          <div class="pt-pending-badge mono">measurement pending</div>
          <p>
            No model roster has been run against the
            {' '}<span class="mono">{canteen.verticalId}</span> tasks yet, so Canteen carries no score
            on this page. Results appear here when a sweep completes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pt-cta">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Build the suite for your ecosystem</h2>
      <p>
        If you run a developer platform and want to know what coding agents can actually build on it,
        the method transfers. We read what your community ships, author tasks from the patterns that
        recur, calibrate each one three ways, and publish the results with their coverage attached.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-cta-row">
        <a class="pt-btn" href="mailto:hello@tangle.tools?subject=Ecosystem%20benchmark">hello@tangle.tools</a>
        <a class="pt-btn ghost" href="/partners/arc">See the Arc task ladder &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .shell { width: min(72rem, 92vw); margin: 0 auto; }
  .mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-feature-settings: 'tnum'; }

  .pt-hero { background: var(--paper-1); padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); }
  .pt-back { color: #4F46E5; font-size: 0.9rem; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; }
  .pt-back:hover { color: #4338CA; }
  .pt-role { margin-top: 1.4rem; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .pt-hero h1 { margin: 0.4rem 0 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.035em; color: var(--ink); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); }
  .pt-lede { margin: 1.1rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.4vw, 1.28rem); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 50rem; }
  .pt-facts { display: flex; gap: 1.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.6rem; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .pt-facts strong { color: #4F46E5; }

  .pt-body { background: var(--paper-0); padding: 3rem 0 2rem; }
  .pt-block { margin-bottom: 3.2rem; scroll-margin-top: 2rem; }
  .pt-block h2, .pt-cta h2 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.7rem; }
  .pt-p { margin: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 52rem; }
  .pt-note { margin: 0.9rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 52rem; }
  .pt-note .mono { color: var(--ink-secondary); }

  .pt-method-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .pt-m { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem; box-shadow: 0 8px 26px rgba(25,28,60,0.05); }
  .pt-m h3 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .pt-m p { margin: 0.55rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .pt-m .mono { color: var(--ink); font-size: 0.84rem; word-break: break-all; }

  .pt-receipts-scroll { margin-top: 1.5rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(25,28,60,0.06); }
  .pt-receipts { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 48rem; }
  .pt-receipts thead th { text-align: left; padding: 0.8rem 1rem; color: var(--ink-muted); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); white-space: nowrap; }
  .pt-receipts tbody td { padding: 0.65rem 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); color: var(--ink-secondary); vertical-align: middle; }
  .pt-receipts tbody tr:first-child td { border-top: none; }
  .pt-r-id { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pt-r-num { color: #4F46E5; font-weight: 700; }
  /* share-of-corpus bar: width is the real share, so the column reads as a distribution */
  .pt-r-bar-cell { min-width: 11rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .pt-bar { display: block; height: 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; background: #4F46E5; width: calc(var(--f) * 8rem); min-width: 2px; }
  .pt-bar-val { color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .pt-task-ids { color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .pt-none { color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.76rem; }

  .pt-rungs { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.8rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .pt-rung { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); border-radius: 15px; padding: 1.3rem 1.4rem; box-shadow: 0 8px 26px rgba(25,28,60,0.05); }
  .pt-rung-tight { padding: 1rem 1.2rem; }
  .pt-rung-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .pt-rung-head h3 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .pt-rung-count { margin-left: auto; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .pt-chips { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 0.7rem; }
  .pt-chip { font-size: 0.74rem; color: #4F46E5; background: rgba(79,70,229,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(79,70,229,0.2); padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 6px; }

  .pt-pending { margin-top: 1.5rem; border: 1px dashed var(--hairline-light); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--paper-1); padding: 2rem 1.6rem; }
  .pt-pending-badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--ink-muted); background: var(--paper-2); padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem; border-radius: 999px; }
  .pt-pending p { margin: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 48rem; }

  .pt-cta { background: var(--paper-1); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); padding: 3.5rem 0 4.5rem; }
  .pt-cta p { margin: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 48rem; }
  .pt-cta-row { display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .pt-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; padding: 0.55rem 1.05rem; border-radius: 9px; background: #4F46E5; color: #fff; transition: background 0.15s; }
  .pt-btn:hover { background: #4338CA; }
  .pt-btn.ghost { background: transparent; color: #4F46E5; border: 1px solid rgba(79,70,229,0.35); }
  .pt-btn.ghost:hover { background: rgba(79,70,229,0.06); }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .pt-block h2, .pt-cta h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
    .pt-rung-count { margin-left: 0; }
  }
</style>
